  "scoring_notes": [
    "Byte ranges are zero-based half-open UTF-8 source offsets. They identify exact occurrences, not output offsets.",
    "Check that protected occurrences survive in source order with exact payload spelling, punctuation and case. Separate repeated annotations require separate retained occurrences.",
    "Require whole-token boundaries for isolated literal or numeric tokens; a matching substring inside another word is not preservation.",
    "Quote and code delimiters are excluded where only the inner payload is literal; changing curly quotes to straight quotes does not by itself violate these annotations.",
    "Sentence punctuation outside an annotated payload may vary. Punctuation inside URLs, identifiers, code and explicitly quoted literal payloads is protected.",
    "Report protected-string fidelity separately from adjudicated semantic harm. A numeric formatting change can fail exact source fidelity without changing the underlying fact.",
    "These annotations supplement full semantic gold and cannot establish that all remaining words are safe to delete.",
    "Empty arrays mean no additional exact-string checks, not permission to rewrite or delete content.",
    "Accidental removable repeats are not protected. Meaningful repeated numeric/literal occurrences are each protected.",
    "The single explicit name annotation is manually authored for this known case. It makes no claim that arbitrary names are deterministically detectable."
  ],
